{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge","id":1065711,"title":"[2E Fan] Valkyrie Mot as Lodge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-21T06:19:14-07:00","id":1065711,"title":"[2E Fan] Valkyrie Mot as Lodge","content":"( Note: <b>Blasphemies </b>book points Mots as Norse based Lodges variants, so Valkyrie are Lodges in this conversion. It\u2019s also based on lore from <i>Wolf and Raven</i> <b>Dark Era</b> and 2E <b>Werewolf</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1046705-dark-eras-mother-wolf-for-norse-uratha\">changes to genders of God Parents of Uratha</a>. )<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Valkyrie Mot - Choosers of the Slain</b></span><br /> <i>Our proud name and legend is tainted by human myth and fancy. They would have you believe our grandmothers </i><i>were flying about on the backs of grass-eating horses garbed in chrome breastplates and winged helmets. They </i><i>know nothing of us \u2014 most even mistake the fact that the Old Norse for \u201cvalkyrie horse\u201d </i><i>was a play on words for wolf. This much they got right \u2014 when the wolves and ravens came to feed </i><i>among the battle dead, we were not far behind.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Odin, humanity\u2019s All Father, did not die. Long before the Uratha were cast out from gods grace by killing Angerboda, Mother of Wolves, he journeyed to the base of the World Tree at the heart of the Shadow and found the Well of Prophecy. Only sacrifice could stir its waters, so he dug out his right eye so that he could see the future of the universe. There, painted in blood, he saw a last battle far in the future, when the fetters that hold back the Idigams would be sundered and the fate of the world would depend upon one apocalyptic battle. He knew what he must do. He did not flinch from his painful sacrifice, neither do we. He then went to Mani, our own father, and talked like both parents, concerned with fate of all Nine Realms.</i><br /> <br /> <i>To us, Odin\u2019s adopted daughters, he gave the task of finding the best for him. Thus, we are called Summis-urdu, the Choosers of the Slain. That is our sacred duty, to send the greatest warriors to join his hall. At the death of a mighty warrior, we come to perform the Funeral Rite and speed them to the All-Father, preparing for the Final Battle. Of course, we, too, will join with All-Fathers army when the time comes to slay Idigams and their lot, and, for that reason, we must master the arts of war as well.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Sometimes, only when in great need, our elders may call us to fight together for some cause. For this reason, we often train together, to learn our own special arts of war. Know this: when the Valkyries go to war, we go to victory, or to the hall of all dead.</i><br /> <br /> Mot of Valkyrie is sisterhood that had its beginnings in ancient Scandinavia, whene stories of Norse people only take first shape. Great prophecy of Odin was a tale that start to gather female Uratha and Wolf-Blooded warriors shield maidens that wanted to prepare their kind for the Ragnar\u00f6k, the Final Battle. They commune with Odin by the ancient spirit called Valkyrja, that is said to be first of their kind.<br /> <br /> Adherents are women driven by duty and understanding that All Fathers army will let to stop armies of Idigams in future apocalypse. For this, they search great and renowned heroes, to collect their souls for this last stand to come and send them to join forces of Odin. They also become paragons of female Uratha on the North, sacred order of the sisters that fight with dead itself.<br /> <br /> Mot is dedicated to seeking souls of heroes and traditional burial practices, so it\u2019s not a surprise they are in large part composed of Bone Shadows members, taking role for \u2018Angels of Death\u2019 and following Odin and Kamduis-Ur examples in their practice. Rest of the group hails from Storm Lords, cultivating proud traditions of their ancestors and always looking for hidden Claimed posing as recently fallen dead hero \u2013 phenomena known as <i>Draugr</i>. Many point to group\u2019s similarities with Lodge of Arms as Pillar of Iron Masters, but Valkyrie answer they are under guidance of Odin, not man, so they follow their own traditions.<br /> <br /> [For more on the Mot, see p. 101 of <b>Blasphemies</b> book]<br /> <br /> <b>TOTEM: Valkyrja</b><br /> The spirit that oversees the Choosers of the Slain is a fierce, driven but silent in kind. It manifests in a form that\u2019s almost woman-like, with a feminine curves and lines, under great, powerful armor and armed with spear, shield and sword, accompanied by few ravens. But spirit rides not the horse as myths suggest, but majestic Urshul of grey fur. Adherents suspect that Lunacy wraps image of great beast in minds of mortal to popular and harmless kind known from stories. Other abnormality of spirit is that human-like figure has always covered face by winged great helmet. Anyone seeing directly in Totem\u2019s face see she does not have eyes, only two pale lights in their place, like two hunting soul trying to free themselves from her body.<br /> <br /> Valkyrja is dedicated to war and dead, obsessed with battle fields and \u2018decent death\u2019. Spirit looks over passing of souls to their proper afterlife in Valhalla, if they lead good life. She is also far removed from her adherents, leaving a considerable distance for the work of gathering souls, contacting directly only in most dire situations. Mot see their Totem on great battle fields and in silence they do their duties. Most of communication between adherents and Valkyria is done by several ancestor-spirits that serve as this lesser messengers, usually given the customary names of Brynhildr, Freja, G\u00f6ll, G\u00f6ndul, Gudr, Gunn, Herfjoturr, Hildr, Hladgunnr, Hlokk, Hrist, Sigrdrifa, Sigr\u00fan and Svafa. The Valkyrie regard the <i>aurora borealis</i> as a portent of their ancestor-spirits\u2019 approval. But the Valkyrie also often study flocks of ravens regarding the habits of local wolves, if present, looking for signs of their benefactors\u2019 approval and desires. Many Valkyrie care for ravens and feed them to keep them nearby.<br /> <br /> Mot fulfil their duties to Valkyrie by making sure that virtues ( by Norse standards, i.e. Renowns ) people and werewolves will join Odin\u2019s army. Lodges Totem cannot be everywhere \u2013 only on greatest battlefields \u2013 and it\u2019s adherents duty to collect as much great warriors they can. They look for souls of most close associated by their life with Renowns and collect their souls in the moment of death by making their Rite of Funeral.<br /> <br /> <b>Influences of Valkyrie Totem</b>: Death 4, War 3, Wolves 2, Ravens 2<br /> <br /> <b>BONDS</b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Valkyrie Mot are guardians of boundaries between life and death. By this, they can see the restless dead - like ghosts \u2013 anytime they would normally see spirits in Twilight. They can also sense if particular Urged or Claimed is instead driven by dead clinging too much to living.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To find and send souls of those high in Renowns \u2013 i.e. Uratha with Renown 3+ and humans or Wolf-Blooded that could would be marked by the deeds if they were Uratha<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> A Lodge member must at least once per month send soul of one close to Renowns.<br /> <br /> <b>SACRED HUNT</b><br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to detect nearby dying character close to Renowns within a number of miles equal to half his Primal Urge, rounded up.<br /> <br /> <b>TOOLS</b><br /> Valkyrie's Children may purchase the Lodge Armory, Lodge Connections and Lodge Sorcery Merits.<br /> <br /> ( Section to come )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-04-2018, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T06:40:13-07:00","id":1065718,"title":"","content":"Will have to see more on what you've planned for, but in the mean time...<br /> <br /> I'm surprised that you chose &quot;the Valkyrie&quot; as the totem, considering there were supposed to me many of them, and Lodge totems are usually unique aren't they? How about choosing some famous valkyrie, an aspect of Odin, or maybe Odin himself as the totem? And have &quot;Valkyries&quot; be the Lodge members' nicknames?<br /> <br /> Oh, and if these guys are gunning for the Claimed, how about alluding more of the Jotunn who chained Fenris-Ur? Even if you don't use that plot hook since it's technically non-canon, those Jotunn are still Hive-Claimed, and Hive-Claimed are 1) implied to be the source of mortal myths on giants, at least from the Werewolf perspective, and 2) closely related to the idigam in the sense that the idigam are the only confirmed cases of beings capable of creating them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:09:16-07:00","id":1065736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1065718#post1065718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised that you chose &quot;the Valkyrie&quot; as the totem, considering there were supposed to me many of them, and Lodge totems are usually unique aren't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>2E Lodges need singular Totem as patron to work as Spirit Cult they are mechaniclly. Valkyrie Mot from 1E had many ancestors-spirits patrons ( see Totem section above or in <b>Blasphemies</b> ), so I needed to focus on one spirit as proper 'Lodge creator'. She is treated as 'Valkyries Mother' and her lesser ancestors-spirits are day-to-day patrons of particular Lodges gatherings. This way we can have many lesser 'valkyrie spirits' ( mentioned in text ), and still have singular spirit that is proper, but distant, Totem. Think here on relations of Firstborns and Uratha Tribes - most of the time Firstborn do not care everyday workings of Tribe or particular member. He just sends member of his <i>umia</i> as messenger and represntative. It's the same with Valkyrie and her own 'brood'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1065718#post1065718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about choosing some famous valkyrie, an aspect of Odin, or maybe Odin himself as the totem? And have &quot;Valkyries&quot; be the Lodge members' nicknames?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits are less people, more general concepts. You can have all the tales about Luna ( or Mani in Norse setting ), but it still be general spirit of Moon. Ephemeral copy of famous characters are more Goetia part of CoD cosmology.<br /> <br /> As to Odin and using of god in general - the <i>Wolf and Raven</i> Dark Era alludes that even if some Shadow spirits have direct relations to Norse myths - like Mani, Sol or Fenris Ur - rest of the Norse gods can be just nothing more than tales people in Scandinavia tell to themselves. Even if myself I would make them more as Astrals Goetia of particular concepts, it's still that official stand of <b>Dark Eras</b> it's more that Norse gods are just tales for the humans, nowhere to encounter in <i>Hisil</i>. You could, for example, meet Thuderer as looking somehow similiar to Thor from local legends, but in Shadow Realm you will not meet 'The Thor'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf and Raven Dark Era</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming into this period, almost all Scandinavians arepagans in the sight of their Christian neighbors, worshiping the Aesir and the Vanir. These are not the distant gods of other faiths, but living beings who wander this world and others pursuing their own agendas and creating new stories.<br /> The religion centers on Uppsala, a holy site where pilgrimage and sacrifices are made every nine years. More regular sacrifice, bl\u00f3t, is made around each solstice and equinox. Despite their own knowledge of the Shadow and its deities, the Forsaken are none the wiser about the nature of the gods of Asgard. Some worship out of tradition or political convenience, regarding genuine faith as leaning towards the Flesh. But almost all revere Mani, the moon god, as an embodiment of Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Genuine faith leaning towards to Flesh' implying that literal worship of gods is 'non-Spirit', i.e. gods are not part of Shadow Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1065718#post1065718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and if these guys are gunning for the Claimed, how about alluding more of the Jotunn who chained Fenris-Ur? Even if you don't use that plot hook since it's technically non-canon, those Jotunn are still Hive-Claimed, and Hive-Claimed are 1) implied to be the source of mortal myths on giants, at least from the Werewolf perspective, and 2) closely related to the idigam in the sense that the idigam are the only confirmed cases of beings capable of creating them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for idea, I will over if putting Jotunn somewhere in write-up will have sense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-21-2017, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:25:55-07:00","id":1065942,"title":"","content":"Okay, so let\u2019s go in to Tools of Valkyrie Mot. First is\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Funeral Rites</b></span><br /> <br /> Heart and soul of Mot\u2019s duties is performing service for dying or dead warriors, sending their souls to Valhalla to join the Odin\u2019s army. They do this by invoking so called Funeral Rites, last soul\u2019s anointing before going to second world. They are also done to free the corpses from any spiritual influence. There are two versions of Rite \u2013 one is of Wolf kind, for battle situations. Another is Pack one, where whole pack comes to send fallen hero in his last journey.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Funeral Wolf Rite (\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> A gift of living to the dead, rite assures that souls move to afterlife and body is cleansed of other influences.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Death, journey, deeds<br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> On the battlefield, Valkryie kneel beside the target of Rite, takes his head in her hands and recite his Renowns, calling Odin All Father to claim his soul. ( Presence + Expression )<br /> <b>Modifiers:</b> Renown that target earn in live and invoked in recitation +1<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant ( 3 successes; roll represents 1 turn of recitation )<br /> <b>Success:</b> Soul of the dead is send to Afterlife. If there is Ephemeral Entity taken power over body, it\u2019s Manifestations are ended and Entity linger in the Twilight near the body. Being rolls her Rank to contrast roll of Ritemaster. If he wins, Entity lost it\u2019s ties to body and linger near to it in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Funeral Pack Rite (\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> This Funeral Rite is performed when there is a time to make proper funeral ceremony. This version of Rite is much more powerful, but it\u2019s also let the target lay at least few hours, suspended between life and death. It\u2019s also more effective in banishing bad forces from it.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Death, journey, deeds<br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> Running of the Rite is local culture funeral ceremony, lead by the Ritemaster. In Norse culture, it\u2019s typical \u2018Viking funeral\u2019 scenes. (Presence + Expression)<br /> <b>Modifiers:</b> Renown that target earn in live and invoked in recitation +1<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (10 successes; each roll represents 15 minutes)<br /> <b>Success: </b>Soul of the dead is send to Afterlife. If there is Ephemeral Entity taken power over body, it\u2019s Manifestations are ended and Entity linger in the Twilight near the body. Being rolls her Rank to contrast roll of Ritemaster. If he wins, Entity lost it\u2019s ties to body and linger near to it in Twilight. Additionally, all participants are cleansed from foreign influence of Ephemerals also \u2013 treat all Pack members taking part in ceremony as the targets of above power.<br /> <br /> <br /> Example scene of invoking Funeral Rite in Norse community by Valkiries whole Pack. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mp6PbopiAvQ\" data-code=\"Mp6PbopiAvQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Mp6PbopiAvQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:36:51-07:00","id":1066030,"title":"","content":"I was more about spirits claiming themselves to be the source of human faiths, like how the Thunderer can claim himself to be Zeus, Indra, Thor and such. Rather than spirits really being that person/god, since then that'd make them closer to Goetia like you said. So in this case, the lodge's totem is &quot;the&quot; Valkyrie, who commands lesser 'valkyries', right?<br /> <br /> On the funeral rites: So they're basically exorcism in function? Hmm... how did the Pass On (name?) Ceremony in Geist work again? I was expecting something closer to that - sending the fallen hero's ghost to the 'true' afterlife. Ending their Manifestations just send them to the Underworld, which the Norse would associate with Helheim. And heroes don't go to Helheim.<br /> <br /> How do this guys interact with the einherjar? Since this is Werewolf, they're likely ancestor spirits. Can the lodge summon them in times of great need?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:50:17-07:00","id":1066040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1065942#post1065942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Success:</b> Soul of the dead is send to Afterlife. If there is Ephemeral Entity taken power over body, it\u2019s Manifestations are ended and Entity linger in the Twilight near the body. Being rolls her Rank to contrast roll of Ritemaster. If he wins, Entity lost it\u2019s ties to body and linger near to it in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're going to pay Experience for a rite at least have it be useful, it should send any ghost onward to the great beyond, not just temporarily end manifestations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T17:11:26-07:00","id":1066052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066030#post1066030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was more about spirits claiming themselves to be the source of human faiths, like how the Thunderer can claim himself to be Zeus, Indra, Thor and such. Rather than spirits really being that person/god, since then that'd make them closer to Goetia like you said. So in this case, the lodge's totem is &quot;the&quot; Valkyrie, who commands lesser 'valkyries', right?<br /> <br /> On the funeral rites: So they're basically exorcism in function? Hmm... how did the Pass On (name?) Ceremony in Geist work again? I was expecting something closer to that - sending the fallen hero's ghost to the 'true' afterlife. Ending their Manifestations just send them to the Underworld, which the Norse would associate with Helheim. And heroes don't go to Helheim.<br /> <br /> How do this guys interact with the einherjar? Since this is Werewolf, they're likely ancestor spirits. Can the lodge summon them in times of great need?</div> </div> </div> </div>oi wait gods arent spirits of a higher level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T17:29:20-07:00","id":1066060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066052#post1066052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> oi wait gods arent spirits of a higher level?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many, many things in the world that can claim themselves to be gods. Even if you don't go crossover, we have both the spirit lords of the Shadow and chthonic ghost-gods of the Underworld, both of which can claim divinity. Go a little sideways, and werewolves can dream themselves to the Dreaming Earth, which is a section of the Astral Realms where archetypical gods born out of the World's dreams dwell. (Mages call these spirits of the Astrals as Goetia, but werewolves probably don't care.) There are also hints that a werewolf who attains Primal Urge 10 may metamorphosize into something stranger, more akin to the Pangaeans of old. Oh, and we can't forget the <i>idigam</i>.<br /> <br /> And if we do go full crossover, let's see... high-Rank angels of the God-Machine, Supernal entities, Abyssal entities, archmages, Dominions of the Inferno, other <i>acathartoi </i>of the Lower Depths (including some particularly potent Strix), really ancient vampires, <i>qashmallim</i>, True Fae, the Judges of Duat, some Beasts who attained Inheritance...<br /> <br /> Whether any of those things above really are divine is up to how you define divinity. But many people would, and a good number of them sure see themselves as gods. And they aren't too keen on someone criticizing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  typo 03-21-2017, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T17:44:01-07:00","id":1066068,"title":"","content":"Thinking back on the first question from 21C Hermit, I was also surprised you abandoned the mot in favor to make a lodge. One suggestion I'd offer is to simply have the lodge be an exception. These exist in the game, and for whatever reason the Lodge might have multiple spirit totems instead of one.<br /> <br /> Another solution that might dovetail with your lodge concept is having one valkyrie spirit per lodge, and each devoted to a different Renown. I'm reading, 'Aspiration: To find and send souls of those close to Renowns.' to mean that the werewolf seeks and sends the soul of a character who acted within the realm of one Renown. So an honorable person or a glorious person. Instead, keeping the 'mot' as a group of lodges, each lodge can have a valkyrie devoted to a different Renown. This way you can get some back and forth conflict between them, too, with werewolves arguing over who the dead 'deserves' to be sent to, the Honorable Valkyrie or the Glorious one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T00:23:39-07:00","id":1066164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066030#post1066030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was more about spirits claiming themselves to be the source of human faiths, like how the Thunderer can claim himself to be Zeus, Indra, Thor and such. Rather than spirits really being that person/god, since then that'd make them closer to Goetia like you said. So in this case, the lodge's totem is &quot;the&quot; Valkyrie, who commands lesser 'valkyries', right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Totem is 'the' Valkyrie, that is Shadow archetype of battlefield death. Lesser valkyries are her Umia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066030#post1066030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the funeral rites: So they're basically exorcism in function? Hmm... how did the Pass On (name?) Ceremony in Geist work again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not know enoguht <b>Geist</b> for this to know. If someone can compare rules for those, I would appreciate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066030#post1066030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was expecting something closer to that - sending the fallen hero's ghost to the 'true' afterlife. Ending their Manifestations just send them to the Underworld, which the Norse would associate with Helheim. And heroes don't go to Helheim.</div> </div> </div> </div>You all assume that only bodies own ghosts is taking control of corpses after death. <i>Wolf and Raven</i> in section on Restless Dead points that is not the case. Many spirits like to flee Shadow using dead mans body as Resonant. OTHER, older ghosts on battlefield would want to use corpses to leave they place of eternal demantion. Not to mention wierder things... It's not a coincidence that I made Storm Lords join Valkyries Lodge to hunt Claimed and other things controlling bodies.<br /> <br /> Helheim is sending place OF GHOSTS, those that died unworthy death ( old age, sickness, etc. ). As I pointed in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1047550-dark-eras-wolf-and-raven-nine-realms?p=1059373#post1059373\">Nine Realms topic</a>, both Helheim and Valhalla are in CoD cosmology as Domains in Underworld. Even then, only small percentage of dead warriors leave ghosts in first place - most souls in death instance goes to Afterlife, whatever it is in reality of CoD ( Remember, Underworld =/= Afterlife ). BUT if mage was looking for souls, any residual soul would left body after Funeral Rite, in <b>Mage</b> terms. Bodies own ghost also.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066030#post1066030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do this guys interact with the einherjar? Since this is Werewolf, they're likely ancestor spirits. Can the lodge summon them in times of great need?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool idea! I will look over rules and prepear probably Rite for summoning Einherjars. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-30-2017, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T00:38:15-07:00","id":1066165,"title":"","content":"Ah, so the exorcism is done to prevent desecration of the fallen warriors' bodies? That I understand well now. <br /> <br /> Dunno much about Geist's mechanics myself, either. So I instead suggest separating the two effects into two rites, instead of having two rites with broad effects. One rite, intended for use mid-battle, would banish malign ghosts and spirits from corpses they possess. And perhaps make the corpse 'sanctified' and unable to be possessed? The other rite, intended for use post-battle, would send off a fallen warrior's soul to Valhalla. When used on a mortal's remains, it prevents him from leaving a ghost and Passes On any ghost already left. When used on a werewolf's remains, it adds the werewolf's personality and prowess to the spiritual amalgam that is the ancestor spirit. <br /> <br /> Don't count on me for rites, though. I haven't read the section on them in detail yet!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T00:41:19-07:00","id":1066167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066040#post1066040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're going to pay Experience for a rite at least have it be useful, it should send any ghost onward to the great beyond, not just temporarily end manifestations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Answered in post above for <b>21Hermit</b>. But want to point once more - Valkyrie Lodge would perform Funeral Rite over the body of great warrior ( or suspected to be inhabited by Ephemeral Entity ). They send bodies souls to Afterlife ( or Valhalla if to Underworld ) and there are left with some spirits or <i>other</i> ghost fettered to corpses. Making Funeral Rite let's them to dislodge entity from corpses - and when Ephemeral is in Twilight, they can hunt it, leaving corpses free of alien influence. Having time, I would suspect most Valkyrie would initiate <b>second</b> Sacred Hunt on the Ephemeral Entity that was using corpses before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T01:06:50-07:00","id":1066172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066068#post1066068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking back on the first question from 21C Hermit, I was also surprised you abandoned the mot in favor to make a lodge. One suggestion I'd offer is to simply have the lodge be an exception. These exist in the game, and for whatever reason the Lodge might have multiple spirit totems instead of one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mots ARE culturally connected Lodges - it was <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1010718-2e-mots\">consensus from previous discussion on this topic</a>. And, really, I made singular Totem only because of mechanics write up of Lodges use them. This, and needed one Influences list to let members choose Lodge Sorcery Merit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066068#post1066068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another solution that might dovetail with your lodge concept is having one valkyrie spirit per lodge, and each devoted to a different Renown. I'm reading, 'Aspiration: To find and send souls of those close to Renowns.' to mean that the werewolf seeks and sends the soul of a character who acted within the realm of one Renown. So an honorable person or a glorious person. Instead, keeping the 'mot' as a group of lodges, each lodge can have a valkyrie devoted to a different Renown. This way you can get some back and forth conflict between them, too, with werewolves arguing over who the dead 'deserves' to be sent to, the Honorable Valkyrie or the Glorious one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could work this way, but I think it would be to niche to work. Remember, we talk here about Lodge that is female only and dedicated to sending dead man to their resting place AND making sure they bodies would be not desecrated by alien forces. We add split over what Renowns to seek, and we end with group that very much can be unplayable in normal chronicle, just because this much specialized it is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I certainly can see each particular adherent favoring seeking one Renown over another, but Lodge, as whole, should stick all great warriors examples for all Five Renowns.<br /> <br /> If you want to run more decentralized Lodge, you can focus each particular group over one Renown, just easily. But I will write them as adhering to Five Renowns in rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-22-2017, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T01:27:28-07:00","id":1066178,"title":"","content":"I want to make simple popular Fetish for Valkyries that can give them knowlegde of fallen heroes actions that makrs him as would-be having Renown just by looking over them. I just do not have particualr idea what it should be, as items. Maybe famous Valkyries Helmets?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066165#post1066165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So I instead suggest separating the two effects into two rites, instead of having two rites with broad effects. One rite, intended for use mid-battle, would banish malign ghosts and spirits from corpses they possess. And perhaps make the corpse 'sanctified' and unable to be possessed?<br /> The other rite, intended for use post-battle, would send off a fallen warrior's soul to Valhalla. When used on a mortal's remains, it prevents him from leaving a ghost and Passes On any ghost already left. When used on a werewolf's remains, it adds the werewolf's personality and prowess to the spiritual amalgam that is the ancestor spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problems I see with this take are those:<br /> 1. This splitting of Funeral Rites means you need to do it <i>twice </i>( mid-battle and post-battle ) and in first place - take all the corpses of the battlefield. I imagine Valkyrie going over <b>many </b>Renowns related dead in battle, to send as many to Valhalla. Then you would need all those corpses to find and make each 'Viking funeral', always. It's A LOT of work considering you have spirits magic.<br /> 2. Even if you would make limited Rite, you would may have too much Ephemeral Entities on battlefield to go after all of them. Remember, Rite is cleansing corpse from Entity influences, but <i>not</i> killing Entity instantly. It's just there, in Twilight, probably ready to run from Valkyries as soon as free. Need of cleaning corpses for second Rite would take too much time and let those Entities to run away.<br /> 3. Having Funeral Rite as both Wolf and Pack Rite let Wolf-Blooded members of Lodge to perform those elaborate 'Viking funerals' when Uratha member is not in vicinity ( probably tracking Ephemeral that run from previous battle ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-22-2017, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T02:53:20-07:00","id":1066204,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Pack Rite \u2013 Call the Einherjar (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> This rite summons up a Einherjar from Odin\u2019s army that was once send to Valhalla by Valkyrie, returning by their call. Bone Shadows Choosers of Slain still debate if Einherjar are really ghosts or ancestor spirits.<br /> <b>Symbols: </b>Circles, a call, deeds, the memento of Einherjar<br /> <b>Sample Rite: </b>Valkyrie prepares summoning of Einherjar by finding memento of his life and reciting his Renowns deeds. She invokes call to the Odin himself, pleading him to release one of his warriors cause he\u2019s help in doing great deeds is needed. ( Presence + Expression)<br /> <b>Modifiers:</b> Renown that target earn in live and invoked in recitation +1<br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (20 successes; each roll represents 1 minute); potentially contested by the Einherjar\u2019s Resistance<br /> <b>Success: </b>This rite targets a particular Einherjar by name. The entity becomes immediately aware once the rite begins, and can try to resist or can voluntarily respond to the call. If the rite succeeds, the Einherjar immediately appears within a delineated summoning spot.<br /> If the summoning takes place in the material world, the area within the delineated space gains the Open Condition and the Einherjar appears in Twilight. If it has the Materialize Manifestation, then it may use this power at no cost when it appears.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Fetish \u2013 Valkyrie\u2019s Helmet (\u2022)</b></span><br /> Famous winged helmets of Valkyries not only protect them from harm to head \u2013 they also convey knowledge of Renown closest deeds of seen person, as they are made of Knowledge spirits.<br /> <b>Effects: </b>Activations of helmet let\u2019s to \u2018hear\u2019 the deeds of observed person in the head of Valkyrie for whole scene. Item also works as proper helmet that not confers typical penalty to Perception roles and having those traits: Rating 2/1, Strength 2, Defense \u20131, Speed 0, Covarage: Head","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-22-2017, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:01:08-07:00","id":1066239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge#post1065711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blessing:</b> Valkyrie Mot are guardians of boundaries between life and death. By this, they can see the restless dead - like ghosts \u2013 anytime they would normally see spirits in Twilight. They can also sense if particular Urged or Claimed is instead driven by dead clinging too much to living.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't have 'can see ghosts in Twilight' as there's a Death Facet that basically already does this and a bit more, meaning the Blessing is not very good for characters that have the Gift of Death. The second part doesn't make much sense as a standalone effect - you can't necessarily tell that a character is Urged or Claimed just by looking at them anyway, but if this *does* detect that then it's basically the Storm Lord Sacred Hunt effect except always on, which isn't a good idea as a Lodge blessing. Finally, 'driven by dead clinging too much to living' is unclear as to what it means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Aspiration:</b> To find and send souls of those close to Renowns. </div> </div> </div>What do you mean, specifically, by close to a Renown? This is pretty important, given that you then run the Ban off the same concept...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ban:</b> A Lodge member must at least once per month send soul of one close to Renowns. </div> </div> </div>Again, need to know what 'close to Renowns' means. Without having that defined, adjudicating whether an adherent has broken the Ban or not is going to be rather hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>SACRED HUNT</b><br /> The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to detect nearby dying character close to Renowns within a number of miles equal to half his Primal Urge, rounded up. </div> </div> </div>This isn't a viable Sacred Hunt effect. It doesn't really make much sense - you go on a Valkyrie Sacred Hunt against your prey, then start pinging on 'close to Renown' characters nearby who have nothing to do with the hunt?<br /> <br /> I would suggest, once you've defined what close to Renown means, that the Hunt effect could work as simply 'you can tell whether the prey is (close to the Renowns/has a Renown rating of 4 or higher/whatever other tool for judging the condition is appropriate).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>TOOLS</b><br /> Valkyrie's Children may purchase the Lodge Armory, Lodge Connections and Lodge Sorcery Merits. </div> </div> </div>Why all of these three Merits? I could see one of Armoury or Sorcery depending on the focus you want to give the Lodge, but I'd only go with one. Lodge Connections seems completely superfluous to the Lodge concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Funeral Rites</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Funeral Wolf Rite (\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> A gift of living to the dead, rite assures that souls move to afterlife and body is cleansed of other influences.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Death, journey, deeds<br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> On the battlefield, Valkryie kneel beside the target of Rite, takes his head in her hands and recite his Renowns, calling Odin All Father to claim his soul. ( Presence + Expression )<br /> <b>Modifiers:</b> Renown that target earn in live and invoked in recitation +1<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant ( 3 successes; roll represents 1 turn of recitation )<br /> <b>Success:</b> Soul of the dead is send to Afterlife. If there is Ephemeral Entity taken power over body, it\u2019s Manifestations are ended and Entity linger in the Twilight near the body. Being rolls her Rank to contrast roll of Ritemaster. If he wins, Entity lost it\u2019s ties to body and linger near to it in Twilight. </div> </div> </div>First up, you need to add the specifications of how this rite can be used and targeted; if there's a limitation on how long dead the target corpse can be, etc. The mechanics don't quite make sense for the contest with punting a corpse-jacking entity out either. 'Being rolls her Rank to contrast roll of ritemaster' - which of the ritemaster's rolls? This is, functionally, a combat-time Expel for corpses only; it should probably run off the same basic mechanic as Expel rather than inventing a whole new one.<br /> <br /> Should have four symbols rather than three.<br /> <br /> It is probably worth considerably more than 1 dot. Exactly where on the scales it would fall partly depends on what happens to the soul it affects - where exactly it sends it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Funeral Pack Rite (\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> This Funeral Rite is performed when there is a time to make proper funeral ceremony. This version of Rite is much more powerful, but it\u2019s also let the target lay at least few hours, suspended between life and death. It\u2019s also more effective in banishing bad forces from it.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Death, journey, deeds<br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> Running of the Rite is local culture funeral ceremony, lead by the Ritemaster. In Norse culture, it\u2019s typical \u2018Viking funeral\u2019 scenes. (Presence + Expression)<br /> <b>Modifiers:</b> Renown that target earn in live and invoked in recitation +1<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (10 successes; each roll represents 15 minutes)<br /> <b>Success: </b>Soul of the dead is send to Afterlife. If there is Ephemeral Entity taken power over body, it\u2019s Manifestations are ended and Entity linger in the Twilight near the body. Being rolls her Rank to contrast roll of Ritemaster. If he wins, Entity lost it\u2019s ties to body and linger near to it in Twilight. Additionally, all participants are cleansed from foreign influence of Ephemerals also \u2013 treat all Pack members taking part in ceremony as the targets of above power. </div> </div> </div>'Like this other rite you already have, but a bit different is not a design approach I'd take. I'd suggest entirely cutting this rite.<br /> <br /> Needs three symbols, definitions about hows and whens, etc.<br /> <br /> 'All participants are cleansed from foreign influence of Ephemerals' - you need to be clearer on what you mean by foreign influence here. It's also not entirely clear *why* the rite would copy the expulsion effect across the rest of the pack, given it's not their funeral and they're not dead bodies.<br /> <br /> Again, considerably more than 1 dot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066204#post1066204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Pack Rite \u2013 Call the Einherjar (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> This rite summons up a Einherjar from Odin\u2019s army that was once send to Valhalla by Valkyrie, returning by their call. Bone Shadows Choosers of Slain still debate if Einherjar are really ghosts or ancestor spirits.<br /> <b>Symbols: </b>Circles, a call, deeds, the memento of Einherjar<br /> <b>Sample Rite: </b>Valkyrie prepares summoning of Einherjar by finding memento of his life and reciting his Renowns deeds. She invokes call to the Odin himself, pleading him to release one of his warriors cause he\u2019s help in doing great deeds is needed. ( Presence + Expression)<br /> <b>Modifiers:</b> Renown that target earn in live and invoked in recitation +1<br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (20 successes; each roll represents 1 minute); potentially contested by the Einherjar\u2019s Resistance<br /> <b>Success: </b>This rite targets a particular Einherjar by name. The entity becomes immediately aware once the rite begins, and can try to resist or can voluntarily respond to the call. If the rite succeeds, the Einherjar immediately appears within a delineated summoning spot.<br /> If the summoning takes place in the material world, the area within the delineated space gains the Open Condition and the Einherjar appears in Twilight. If it has the Materialize Manifestation, then it may use this power at no cost when it appears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm missing something, this rite seems redundant. It's Shadowcall, except more limited for the same cost. I would cut it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Fetish \u2013 Valkyrie\u2019s Helmet (\u2022)</b></span><br /> Famous winged helmets of Valkyries not only protect them from harm to head \u2013 they also convey knowledge of Renown closest deeds of seen person, as they are made of Knowledge spirits.<br /> <b>Effects: </b>Activations of helmet let\u2019s to \u2018hear\u2019 the deeds of observed person in the head of Valkyrie for whole scene. Item also works as proper helmet that not confers typical penalty to Perception roles and having those traits: Rating 2/1, Strength 2, Defense \u20131, Speed 0, Covarage: Head </div> </div> </div>The 'famous' winged helmets are, to my understanding, entirely a fabrication of artists over a thousand years later. What does 'hear the deeds' mean - does it recite a litany of the target's accomplishments, like 'And lo, Steve did stab the mighty bear with a spoon until it died, which was mightily Glorious' or is it giving a running commentary of the deeds he's undertaking right now?<br /> <br /> I'd probably redo it as a 3-dot Facet that lets you shift the effect of Know Thy Prey.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Making the Lodge female-only is fairly meaningless, given every Uratha can gain the ability to alter their sex for 1 XP.<br /> <br /> A final note - you seem to have the Mot playing the whole Valkyrie thing pretty straight. It's a shame the Secrets of the Lodges extra material still hasn't gone up, as it'd help illuminate one of the areas of Lodges that probably needs more direct examples - they're cults, all of them. They do weird shit, pursue hidden agendas, and generally have a whole pile of skeletons in the closet. To me, it feels like the Mot are just too... normal? Too nice? Now, on the one hand, this is a bit subverted by their ban - the adherents are gonna end up murdering 'close to Renown' people on a regular basis to sate it, as there just aren't going to be enough battles to feed it anyway. However, were I looking at doing a Valkyrie Lodge, I would make it much clearer and more sinister as to what happens to the poor bastards they 'choose' (and honestly I'd probably say 'the Valkyrie spirit just eats their souls to power it up for the future Ragnarok thing; humans' glorious ideals of Valkyries are a really, really unfortunate misunderstanding of what's really going on).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:26:31-07:00","id":1066249,"title":"","content":"First, I will answer most dire question - <b>What is all about 'close to Renowns' in Lodge write-up?</b><br /> <br /> Well, from my read of 2E corebook, Renowns are ephemeral marks of accomplishment made on Uratha by spirits from particular deeds. So non-Uratha characters cannot have Renowns per se. BUT they still can make famous or important actions that are in accord with Cunning, Glory, Honor, Purity, and Wisdom. Valkyrie looks for those that are mortal or Uratha that makes deeds close to those 'virtues' in moments of death - even if <i>Hisil</i> only marks Uratha as having proper Renowns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066239#post1066239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't have 'can see ghosts in Twilight' as there's a Death Facet that basically already does this and a bit more, meaning the Blessing is not very good for characters that have the Gift of Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not know all Facets ( yet ), but I recall somewhere to read that Blessing that mirrored Gift Facet let you use this Facet for free if character has it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066239#post1066239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second part doesn't make much sense as a standalone effect - you can't necessarily tell that a character is Urged or Claimed just by looking at them anyway, but if this *does* detect that then it's basically the Storm Lord Sacred Hunt effect except always on, which isn't a good idea as a Lodge blessing. Finally, 'driven by dead clinging too much to living' is unclear as to what it means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have other idea on second part of Lodge Blessings then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:34:59-07:00","id":1066251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066249#post1066249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I will answer most dire question - <b>What is all about 'close to Renowns' in Lodge write-up?</b><br /> <br /> Well, from my read of 2E corebook, Renowns are ephemeral marks of accomplishment made on Uratha by spirits from particular deeds. So non-Uratha characters cannot have Renowns per se. BUT they still can make famous or important actions that are in accord with Cunning, Glory, Honor, Purity, and Wisdom. Valkyrie looks for those that are mortal or Uratha that makes deeds close to those 'virtues' in moments of death - even if <i>Hisil</i> only marks Uratha as having proper Renowns.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSure. But you need to have a tighter definition around this for the Lodge, because they have a mechanical penalty - Ban breakage - that relies on it.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo start with, what do you define as 'close to Renown' in an Uratha? How many dots do they need in a Renown to qualify as valid prey?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do not know all Facets ( yet ), but I recall somewhere to read that Blessing that mirrored Gift Facet let you use this Facet for free if character has it. </div> </div> </div>\u200bYes; iirc it's the Lodge of the Screaming Moon that have that effect, so that their benefits don't render a particular Facet redundant. However, the 'can see ghosts in Twilight' aspect of Barghest, the Death Facet in question, is always on and free so there's not much to really improve there.<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides which, I think you need to focus the Lodge a bit more in terms of what their prey is. Is it high-Renown types whose souls they want to send on to the Valkyrie, or is it ephemeral entities possessing corpses of the worthy? I'd suggest picking one or the other and focusing on that, rather than trying to do both mechanically and ending up a bit muddled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:42:57-07:00","id":1066254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066239#post1066239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why all of these three Merits? I could see one of Armoury or Sorcery depending on the focus you want to give the Lodge, but I'd only go with one. Lodge Connections seems completely superfluous to the Lodge concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why only one of Lodge Merits? And why not Connections? Lodge is directly stated in 1E as sisterhood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066239#post1066239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First up, you need to add the specifications of how this rite can be used and targeted; if there's a limitation on how long dead the target corpse can be, etc. The mechanics don't quite make sense for the contest with punting a corpse-jacking entity out either. 'Being rolls her Rank to contrast roll of ritemaster' - which of the ritemaster's rolls? This is, functionally, a combat-time Expel for corpses only; it should probably run off the same basic mechanic as Expel rather than inventing a whole new one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will look over Expel then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066239#post1066239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should have four symbols rather than three.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will look over this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066239#post1066239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is probably worth considerably more than 1 dot. Exactly where on the scales it would fall partly depends on what happens to the soul it affects - where exactly it sends it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To Afterlife or Vallhala ( Underworld Domain ), depending on the Renowns of previous warrior. Afterlife =/= Vallhala. Afterlife is Grrat Beyond, not described in any CoD books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066239#post1066239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I'm missing something, this rite seems redundant. It's Shadowcall, except more limited for the same cost. I would cut it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <i>based</i> on Shadowcall, not Shadowcall itself. Shadowcall is based on spirits, Einherjar are could be ghosts from Underworld, so different beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066239#post1066239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does 'hear the deeds' mean - does it recite a litany of the target's accomplishments, like 'And lo, Steve did stab the mighty bear with a spoon until it died, which was mightily Glorious' or is it giving a running commentary of the deeds he's undertaking right now?</div> </div> </div> </div>First take - it says to wearer head litany of deeds. And I choose Helmets only becuase I needed some iconic items.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066239#post1066239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making the Lodge female-only is fairly meaningless, given every Uratha can gain the ability to alter their sex for 1 XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was all femals only in 1E - and Valkyries are all females in Norse myths. Hmm...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066239#post1066239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now, on the one hand, this is a bit subverted by their ban - the adherents are gonna end up murdering 'close to Renown' people on a regular basis to sate it, as there just aren't going to be enough battles to feed it anyway. However, were I looking at doing a Valkyrie Lodge, I would make it much clearer and more sinister as to what happens to the poor bastards they 'choose' (and honestly I'd probably say 'the Valkyrie spirit just eats their souls to power it up for the future Ragnarok thing; humans' glorious ideals of Valkyries are a really, really unfortunate misunderstanding of what's really going on).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not understand you here. Could you describe it in some simpler way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:48:34-07:00","id":1066258,"title":"","content":"After reading Acrozatarim's posts, I suggest the Sacred prey be something that can include &quot;Uratha with Renown 4+&quot; and &quot;humans and Wolf-Blooded who earn Renown, despite it now showing up as spirit-brands.&quot;<br /> <br /> How about tweaking the Rites you came up with as Acrozatarim said, and generalize them so that they're new homebrew Rites available to any Uratha should they come across it? Of course, the Valkyries would have them foremost, but this way other death-focused packs and lodges could learn them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:50:25-07:00","id":1066260,"title":"","content":"What Acrozatarim meant on the part you said didn't understand was that, basically, make these guys a cult and not a sorority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T06:39:27-07:00","id":1066275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066260#post1066260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Acrozatarim meant on the part you said didn't understand was that, basically, make these guys a cult and not a sorority.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are cult that is sisterhood. I really do not understand problem with that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066258#post1066258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading Acrozatarim's posts, I suggest the Sacred prey be something that can include &quot;Uratha with Renown 4+&quot; and &quot;humans and Wolf-Blooded who earn Renown, despite it now showing up as spirit-brands.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Renown 4+ is too much - literally, it would one, maybe two characters per whole chronicle in places with low Uratha number. I think that maybe good balance could be Renown 3+ characters. And just 'humans and Wolf-Blooded that could would be marked by the deeds if they were Uratha'. Humans and Wolf-Blooded <i>do not</i> have proper Renowns like werewolves ( at least from my reading of 2E corebook ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066258#post1066258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about tweaking the Rites you came up with as Acrozatarim said, and generalize them so that they're new homebrew Rites available to any Uratha should they come across it? Of course, the Valkyries would have them foremost, but this way other death-focused packs and lodges could learn them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are Rites, they are always able to be reinterpreted if you like. I will fix them later today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T07:01:22-07:00","id":1066283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066275#post1066275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are cult that is sisterhood. I really do not understand problem with that....</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course a cult can be a sisterhood at the same time. However, lodges are cults of the hunt foremost. Unless your definition of a sisterhood involves shadowy meetings hostile to outside inquiries, worship of a spirit and serving its inscrutable ends, odd rituals that make no rational sense to outsiders, and morally questionable practices, I'd say the cult aspect is lacking.<br /> <br /> Look at <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1056100-lodge-of-the-seven-venoms-draft\">this draft of the Lodge of the Seven Venoms</a>. Just looking at the mechanics, they're just master poisoners and alchemists. Strange, but nothing special. But look at the not-yet-revealed fluff part just above the mechanics:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Generally the Seven Venoms aren't looked well upon because their weirdness and bizarreness too easily leaks past attempts at maintaining a normal veneer. I won't write up a full Secrets of the Seven Venoms list of the batshit and heretical stuff they do as I want to keep that under my hat for my poor player, but suffice to say there are all sorts of rumours about how they keep menageries of poisoned (not poisonous) animals that they feed their own flesh and blood to, that they undertake horrific Essence alchemy experiments involving turning human victims into Resonance-tanks of befouled blood, that they don't just carve off pieces of their own flesh but pieces of their own mind, that they mutilate themselves in order to slice off warping fragments of their flesh and spirit that would otherwise bud the very Host Shards they've consumed back out of them, etc etc. Some say they actively and intentionally make Hosts somehow, processing the consumed Shards for some great and nightmarish project. </div> </div> </div><i>That's </i>what a cult looks like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Renown 4+ is too much - literally, it would one, maybe two characters per whole chronicle in places with low Uratha number. I think that maybe good balance could be Renown 3+ characters. And just 'humans and Wolf-Blooded that could would be marked by the deeds if they were Uratha'. Humans and Wolf-Blooded <i>do not</i> have proper Renowns like werewolves ( at least from my reading of 2E corebook ).. </div> </div> </div>Hmm, yeah 4+ could be too much.<br /> <br /> Or you could spin it more interestingly. Tweaking the Ban so that the interval between killin- er, I mean, sending off heroes to Valhalla is shorter. A rite that utters a litany of the hero's great deeds, temporarily raising his Renown and thereby qualifying him for the Hunt. Or just pushing and encouraging promising warriors to become heroes and raise their Renown, so the lodge can harvest them later.<br /> <br /> And of course humans and Wolf-Blooded don't take Renown. I only meant that as a potential expansion the lodge could take in selecting its Sacred Prey. I should have types &quot;humans and Wolf-Blooded who <b>could </b>earn Renown if they werer Uratha.&quot; But then again, there's almost no way to represent this via mechanics, so this may be a moot point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T07:04:49-07:00","id":1066285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066251#post1066251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBesides which, I think you need to focus the Lodge a bit more in terms of what their prey is. Is it high-Renown types whose souls they want to send on to the Valkyrie, or is it ephemeral entities possessing corpses of the worthy? I'd suggest picking one or the other and focusing on that, rather than trying to do both mechanically and ending up a bit muddled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not want to overspecialize Valkyries - hunting for high Renown targets are made mostly on battle-fields. Targeting only Ephemeral Entities possesing corpses of worthy is done only on specific circumstances. Choosing one over another would led to many time Valkyrie would not have many things to do in particular chronicle. Also, both those things are interrelated, as I pointed before - hunting for 'worthy warriors' easily can lead to finding corpses possesed by Ephmeral Entities. Second part is why I think Storm Lords in group.<br /> <br /> And if I can be frank, sometimes I think that example Lodges in <b>The Pack</b> are non-specialized to use them in game in first place - which is their benefit. Thousand Steel Teeth is great to use anytime you are making story in roads and highways - on modern times - everywhere. Lodge of the Screaming Moon just need to defeat their pray screaming. Eaters of the Dead hunt any undead and only need to take corpses care off. Then for Valkyrie going only for 'High Renown targets' will be too focused in my POV - more, <i>Wolf and Raven</i> points that Restless Dead are a big problem in Viking Era. So main focus on High Renown and side job to take care of corpses - seems good fit then. Other way it will be only 'Lodge of Arms or Eaters of Dead clone'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, making Valkyrie Lodge questionable ( by killing high Renown individuals ) and giving them positive side job ( getting rid off Ephemeral Entietis over corpses ) makes them more complex, niuanced and grey area than 'they kill people for Odin, period'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-22-2017, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T07:41:21-07:00","id":1066300,"title":"","content":"The current problem is that you're putting too much mechanical emphasis on the exorcism part. Yes, it's just a Blessing and maybe some tools, but even that's too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:31:46-07:00","id":1066375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge?p=1066300#post1066300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current problem is that you're putting too much mechanical emphasis on the exorcism part. Yes, it's just a Blessing and maybe some tools, but even that's too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's not their primary goal, but they would use it, often. I think I can take out Blessing, but would leave a Rite or two. Lodge is not only it's own main goal, it's also it's culture, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T07:23:41-07:00","id":1095898,"title":"","content":"Re-worded Mot's Aspirations to work with the basic idea of Sacred Hunt more:<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration</b>: To find and send souls of those high in Renowns \u2013 i.e. Uratha with Renown 3+ and humans or Wolf-Blooded that could would be marked by the deeds if they were Uratha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:31:45-07:00","id":1214173,"title":"","content":"With new inspirations from <b>God of War</b> game and pointing to the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-dead-belong-below-geist-the-sin-eaters/\" target=\"_blank\">Reapers ghosts from 2E Underworld</a> - I think about re-focusing Valkyrie Mot in 2E a bit. If we assume that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1208544-2e-dead-dominions-and-folklore?p=1208800#post1208800\">Valhalla is Dead Dominion of Underworld</a> ( as it is pointed in <i>Wolf &amp; Raven</i> Dark Era ), than Odin, for whom Mot is working, is Kerberoi. That would lead to the Valkyrie being, de facto, werewolf version of Reapers ghosts. 'Dead Belong Below' and all of that.<br /> <br /> Valkyrie quest in <b>God of War </b>( 2018 ):<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MIxVpt14Agg\" data-code=\"MIxVpt14Agg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/MIxVpt14Agg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}